# Changes to the contract that no artifact shows, oldest first.
#
# Some changes reach extensions without changing a CRD, the HTTP API or the
# Go API of the contract packages: code that imposes a new requirement on
# extensions, or gives a field they already write a new meaning. Record
# such a change as an entry below, on a line of its own:
#
#   - #<pull request>: <what changed, and what extensions must do>
#
# then run make gen-contract. The entries are part of the contract's
# fingerprint, so the contract version moves as it does for any other
# contract change; these comments are not, so editing them moves nothing.
# A line that is neither blank, a comment ("# ...") nor an entry fails
# make gen-contract, so nothing meant as an entry can fail to count. See
# README.md.
